<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Anglo-Afghan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839–1842</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Anglo-Afghan War was fought between the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. In 1839 a British army, marching through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, invaded, deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dost-mohammad-khan">Dost Mohammad Khan</a> and installed Shah Shuja. A revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> destroyed the retreating British garrison in January 1842. After a punitive expedition the British withdrew, and Dost Mohammad returned to the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-anglo-afghan-war.jpg" alt="First Anglo-Afghan War" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_army_of_the_Indus_entering_Kandahar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
